[00:06.44] I am just a poor boy
[00:08.06] Though my story's seldom told
[00:11.06] I have squandered my resistance
[00:13.72] For a pocketful of mumbles
[00:16.12] Such are promises
[00:19.58] All lies and jest
[00:21.34] Still a man hears what he wants to hear
[00:24.32] And disregards the rest
[00:36.08] When I left my home and my family
[00:38.54] I was no more than a boy
[00:41.00] In the company of strangers
[00:43.94] In the quiet of the railway station
[00:46.92] Running scared
[00:49.92] Laying low, seeking out the poorer quarters
[00:54.20] Where the ragged people go
[00:56.74] Looking for the places only they would know
